1
00:00:00,650 --> 00:00:03,169
A paper ribbon climbs across a bright
landscape.

2
00:00:03,169 --> 00:00:07,263
Its slope becomes gentler until the path
appears flat, and a small marker

3
00:00:07,263 --> 00:00:08,522
pauses at that point.

4
00:00:15,650 --> 00:00:18,228
The ribbon bends downward after the pause.

5
00:00:18,228 --> 00:00:23,383
Now the flat point looks like a summit,
because nearby values rise before it

6
00:00:23,383 --> 00:00:24,856
and fall after it.

7
00:00:30,650 --> 00:00:34,347
Another ribbon falls into a bowl and then
rises again.

8
00:00:34,347 --> 00:00:39,153
Its lowest point also has zero slope, but
it tells a completely different

9
00:00:39,153 --> 00:00:39,522
story.

10
00:00:45,650 --> 00:00:48,276
A third path flattens briefly and
continues climbing.

11
00:00:48,276 --> 00:00:52,543
The marker never reaches a summit or
valley, even though the tangent is

12
00:00:52,543 --> 00:00:53,856
horizontal at the pause.

13
00:01:00,650 --> 00:01:03,665
A frame cuts the landscape into an allowed
interval.

14
00:01:03,665 --> 00:01:08,354
Its edges now matter, because the best
available point may sit directly on a

15
00:01:08,354 --> 00:01:08,689
boundary.

16
00:01:15,650 --> 00:01:21,398
Three flat points remain side by side.
Which one is a maximum, which one is a

17
00:01:21,398 --> 00:01:24,272
minimum, and which one simply continues
its journey?
